          %h4#ClassificationSuperconformal Superconformal and super anti de Sitter symmetry
          %p
            We discuss
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extension"} extensions
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+group"} conformal Lie algebra
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1}
            (equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry"} isometry
            Lie algebra of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+space"} anti de Sitter space
            of dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d+1
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT"} AdS-CFT
          %h5#ClassificationSuperconformalInDim2 In dimension 2
          %p
