            %p
              There exists no
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superconformal"} superconformal
              extension of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 6
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \gt 6
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Shnider88"}> Shnider 88
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Nahm78"} Nahm 78
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Minwalla98"} Minwalla 98, section 4.2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} AdS/CFT correspondence
            see also
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BlencoweDuff88"} Blencowe &amp; Duff 1988
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Duff09"} Duff 2009
            %a{:href => "#Duff21"} Duff 2021
            and see the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Green-Schwarz+action+functional#AsPartOfTheAdSCFTCorrespodence"} super p-brane – As part of the AdS-CFT correspondence
          #ProofOfClassificationOfSuperconformal.proof
            %h6#proof_sketch Proof (sketch)
            %p
              By realizing the conformal real Lie algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(\mathbb{R}^{d,2})
              as a real section of the complexified
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(\mathbb{C}^{d+2})
              one is reduced to finding those (finite dimensional) simple super Lie algebras over the complex numbers whose even-graded part extends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(\mathbb{C}^{d+2})
              and such that the implied
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
              of that on the odd-graded part contains the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            %p
              The complex finite dimensional simple super Lie algebras have been classified, see at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "super+Lie+algebra#Classification"} super Lie algebra – Classification
