                    \\mathfrak{so}(6)\simeq \mathfrak{su}(4) = A_3
            %p
              with the spinor representation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 6
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(6)
              being the vector representation of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔰𝔲
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{su}(4) = A_3
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(3,k)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 6
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 6-2 = 4
            %p
              Finally by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triality"} triality
              the vector representation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(8) = D_4
              is isomorphic to its spinor representation. By the above tables this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 4
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(4,k)
              is a superconformal algebra in dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 8
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 6
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 8-2 = 6
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Shnider88"} Shnider 88, last paragraphs
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Further constraints follow from requiring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-unitary+representations"} super-unitary representations
              (
              %a{:href => "#Minwalla98"}> Minwalla 98, section 4.3
              ). This restricts for instance the 6d superconformal algebra to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 4
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi 𝔬𝔰𝔭
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(4,1) = \mathfrak{osp}(8|2)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 4
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi 𝔬𝔰𝔭
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 8
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(4,1) = \mathfrak{osp}(8,4)
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔰𝔬
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mn 8
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi 𝔬𝔰𝔭
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 6
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(8^\ast|4) = \mathfrak{osp}(6,2|4)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
          %h3#superymmetry_multiplets_and_bps_states Superymmetry multiplets and BPS states
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermultiplet"} supermultiplet
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"} BPS state
          %h3#extensions Extensions
          %p
            In special dimensions supersymmetry super Lie algebras have
            %a{:href => "super%20Poincare%20Lie%20algebra#PolyvectorExtensions"} polyvector extensions
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charges"} charges
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supersymmetry+algebra"} type II supersymmetry algebra
            for the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
            or the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+supersymmetry+algebra"} M-theory supersymmetry algebra
            for the case of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-infinity+algebra"} super L-infinity algebra
            extensions, related to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+6-algebra"} supergravity Lie 6-algebra
            etc. See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+supersymmetry"} extended supersymmetry
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetime"} extended super Minkowski spacetime
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
