            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercharge"} supercharge
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+cycle"} supersymmetric cycle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+representation+of+the+super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} unitary representation of the super Poincaré group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haag%E2%80%93Lopuszanski%E2%80%93Sohnius+theorem"} Haag–Lopuszanski–Sohnius theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+supersymmetry"} extended supersymmetry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superconformal+field+theory"}> superconformal field theory
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vertex+operator+algebra"} super vertex operator algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+supersymmetry"}> hadron supersymmetry
                ,
                %a{:href => "quantum+Hall+effect#ReferencesSupersymmetryInFractionalQuantumHall"} supersymmetry in fractional quantum Hall effect
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"}> supergravity
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring+theory"} superstring theory
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+and+Calabi-Yau+manifolds"} supersymmetry and Calabi-Yau manifolds
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSSM"} MSSM
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "string+theory+FAQ#DoesSTPredictSupersymmetry"} string theory FAQ – Does string theory predict supersymmetry?
          %h2#references References
          %h3#ReferencesHistory History
          %p
            The notion of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%28n%29"} SU(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
            symmetry first appears in the proposal of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+supersymmetry"} hadron supersymmetry
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hironari+Miyazawa"}> Hironari Miyazawa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Baryon Number Changing Currents
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/1235194"} spire:1235194
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1143/PTP.36.1266"} doi:10.1143/PTP.36.1266
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hironari+Miyazawa"}> Hironari Miyazawa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spinor Currents and Symmetries of Baryons and Mesons
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRev.170.1586"} doi:10.1103/PhysRev.170.1586
          %p
            but was ignored (see
            %a{:href => "hadron+supersymmetry#CGNY19"} CGNY 19
            for historical comments).
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré supersymmetry
            was discovered in parallel by two groups in the early 1970s (separated and isolated at that time by “Cold War” nuisances):
          %p
            On the one hand,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Neveu"} André Neveu
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Ramond"} Pierre Ramond
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
            wrote down in 1971 the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            originally called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+string"} spinning string
            – a 2-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
            – and noticed that it just so happens to have an extra graded extension of 2-dimensional Poincaré symmetry. Ever since the previously baptized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+string"} spinning string
            became known as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            (specifically: the
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NSR-superstring"} NSR-superstring
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Neveu"}> André Neveu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Factorizable dual model of pions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(71)90448-2"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(71)90448-2
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Ramond"}> Pierre Ramond
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dual theory for Free Fermions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.3.2415"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.3.2415
          %p
            See also at the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+FAQ"} string theory FAQ
            %em
              %a{:href => "string+theory+FAQ#DoesSTPredictSupersymmetry"} Does string theory predict supersymmetry?
          %p
            Independently, around the same time
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Golfand"} Yuri Golfand
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Evgeny+Likhtman"} Evgeny Likhtman
            in Russia wrote down the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
            in four dimensions:
          %ul
            %li#GolfandLikhtman72
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Golfand"}> Yuri Golfand
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Evgeny+Likhtman"} Evgeny Likhtman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Extensions of the Algebra of the Generators of the Poincaré Group by the Bispinor Generators
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ginzburg"} Victor Ginzburg
                et al. (eds.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em I. E. Tamm Memorial Volume Problems of Theoretical Physics
              %p
                translated and reprinted in:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Shifman"} Mikhail Shifman
                (ed.)
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Many+Faces+of+the+Superworld"} The Many Faces of the Superworld
                pp. 44-53, World Scientific (2000) (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789812793850_0006"}> doi:10.1142/9789812793850_0006
                )
          %p
            This then motivated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julius+Wess"} Julius Wess
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruno+Zumino"} Bruno Zumino
            to study supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theories"} quantum field theories
            in four
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            dimensions:
          %ul
            %li#WessZumino74
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julius+Wess"}> Julius Wess
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruno+Zumino"} Bruno Zumino
              = succeed "," do
                %em Supergauge transformations in four dimensions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814542340_0002"} doi:10.1142/9789814542340_0002
          %p Early review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Fayet"}> Pierre Fayet
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergio+Ferrara"} Sergio Ferrara
              = succeed "," do
                %em Supersymmetry
              %strong 32
              5 (1977) 249-334 [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-1573(77)90066-7"}> doi:10.1016/0370-1573(77)90066-7
              ]
          %p
            From this sprang the idea of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
          %ul
            %li#FerraraZumino74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergio+Ferrara"}> Sergio Ferrara
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruno+Zumino"} Bruno Zumino
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supergauge invariant Yang-Mills theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(74)90559-8"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(74)90559-8
            %li#SalamStrathdee74a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abdus+Salam"}> Abdus Salam
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Strathdee"} John Strathdee
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Super-symmetry and non-Abelian gauges
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(74)90226-3"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(74)90226-3
          %p
            and the early development of the concepts if
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfields"} superfields
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
          %ul
            %li#SalamStrathdee74b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abdus+Salam"}> Abdus Salam
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Strathdee"} John Strathdee
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supergauge Transformations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/89208"} spire:89208
            %li#SalamStrathdee75
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abdus+Salam"}> Abdus Salam
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Strathdee"} John Strathdee
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superfields and Fermi-Bose symmetry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789812795915_0051"} doi:10.1142/9789812795915_0051
          %p#OriginOfTheTerm
            On the origin of the “super”-terminology, from
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#KaneShifman01"} Kane-Shifman 01, p. 4
          %blockquote
            %p
              Often students ask where the name “super-symmetry” came from? It seems that it was coined in the paper by
              %a{:href => "#SalamStrathdee74a"} Salam and Strathdee
              where these authors constructed
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+Yang-Mills+theory"} supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#WessZumino74"} Wess and Zumino
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#WessZumino74"} Wess and Zumino
              %a{:href => "#FerraraZumino74"} Ferrara and Zumino
              (received by the editorial office on May 27, 1974) where the same problem of super-Yang-Mills was addressed, mentions only supergauge invariance and supergauge transformations.
          %p Accounts of the early history of the concept of supersymmetry:
          %ul
            %li#KaneShifman00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"}> Gordon Kane
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Shifman"} Mikhail Shifman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Supersymmetric World: The Beginnings of The Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/4611"} doi:10.1142/4611
              %ul
                %li#KaneShifman01
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"}> Gordon Kane
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Shifman"} Mikhail Shifman
                  %em Introduction to “The Supersymmetric world”
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0102298"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0102298
                  ), chapter in:
                  %a{:href => "#KaneShifman00"} Kane-Shifman 00
            %li#Likhtman01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Evgeny+Likhtman"}> Evgeny Likhtman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Around SuSy 1970
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0101209"} arxiv:hep-ph/0101209
            %li
              %p
