              %em Supersymmetric Dark Matter Candidates
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1001.3651"}> arXiv:1001.3651
              )
          %p
            Supersymmetry seems to be favored by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Starobinsky+model+of+cosmic+inflation"} Starobinsky model of cosmic inflation
            (see there for more).
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            coupled to the (non-supersymmetric)
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cliff+P.+Burgess"}> Cliff P. Burgess
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fernando+Quevedo"} Fernando Quevedo
              %em Who’s Afraid of the Supersymmetric Dark? The Standard Model vs Low-Energy Supergravity
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.13275"}> arXiv:2110.13275
              )
          %h3#supersymmetry_breaking Supersymmetry breaking
          %p
            A review of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+breaking"} supersymmetry breaking
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Yael Shadmi,
              %em Supersymmetry breaking
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0601076"}> arXiv:hep-th/0601076
              )
          %p
            A quantitative analysis showing that locally supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            theories will generically not exhibit global spacetime supersymmetry is
          %ul
            %li#DLSW
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Keith+Dienes"}> Keith Dienes
              , Michael Lennek, David Sénéchal, Vaibhav Wasnik,
              %em Is SUSY Natural?
              NewJ.Phys.10:085003,2008 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0804.4718"}> arXiv:0804.4718
              )
          %h3#experimental_searches Experimental searches
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matt+Reece"}> Matt Reece
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetry: Where do we stand?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.cern.ch/getFile.py/access?contribId=71&sessionId=1&resId=0&materialId=slides&confId=210555"} pdf
            %li#Ellis13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Ellis"}> John Ellis
                ,
                %em Supersymmetric Fits after the Higgs Discovery and Implications for Model Building
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1312.5426"}> arXiv:1312.5426
                )
            %li
              %p
                Pran Nath,
                %em Supersymmetry after the Higgs
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1501.01679"}> arXiv:1501.01679
                )
            %li
              %p
                Nathaniel Craig,
                %em The State of Supersymmetry after Run I of the LHC
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.0528"}> arXiv:1309.0528
                )
            %li
              %p
                Jin Min Yang, Pengxuan Zhu, Rui Zhu,
                %em A brief survey of low energy supersymmetry under current experiments
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.06686"}> arXiv:2211.06686
                )
          %p
            Remembering that there is a considerable difference between global low energy supersymmetry and local higher energy supersymmetry aka
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
          %ul
            %li#Duff04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
              ,
              %em Erice lectures on “The status of local supersymmetry”
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0403160"}> arXiv:hep-th/0403160
              )
          %div
            %h3#emergent_supersymmetry_in_solid_state_physics Emergent supersymmetry in solid state physics
            %h4#general General
            %p
              On
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
              in
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Konstantin Efetov:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Supersymmetry in Disorder and Chaos
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511573057"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511573057
              %li
                %p
                  Sung-Sik Lee:
                  %em TASI Lectures on Emergence of Supersymmetry, Gauge Theory and String in Condensed Matter Systems
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1009.5127"}> arXiv:1009.5127
                  ]
            %h4#quantum_hall_systems Quantum Hall systems
            %p
              For references on emergent supersymmetry in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+Hall+systems"} quantum Hall systems
              see
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "quantum+Hall+effect#ReferencesSupersymmetryInFractionalQuantumHall"} there
